{
 "id": "lem-zl-relative-envelope-factor-reality",
 "blueprint": {
  "is": "lem-zl-relative-envelope-factor-reality",
  "from": null,
  "same_as": null
 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Reality of relative factors for an envelope",
 "statement": "Let $h:U_0\\to Y_0$ be as in [lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual], and\nlet $\\mathcal E$ be lisse, $\\iota$-real, and punctually $\\iota$-pure\nof weight zero. Then every $R^ih_!\\mathcal E$ is $\\iota$-real.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-p-dl-general-relative-line/lem-zl-relative-envelope-factor-reality.md",
  "place": "node lem-zl-relative-envelope-factor-reality, order 2841"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual",
  "def-weil-pbc-qbar-category",
  "def-weil-punctual-weights"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Fix a closed point $y$ of the base. By [thm-cbc-qbar], the\nlocal polynomials of $R^ih_!\\mathcal E$ at $y$ are the polynomials\n$P_i$ of the compactly supported cohomology of the fiber\n$U_{\\bar y}$ (the local Frobenius eigenvalues of the stalk). The\ngroup in degree zero vanishes by (the affine-line form of) the\n$H_c^0$-vanishing of lisse sheaves on nonproper curves,\n[lem-a1-affine-hc0]; the roots of $P_1$ have modulus\nat most $q_y^{1/2}$ by [lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual] (weight\nzero, $i=1$), while every nonzero root of $P_2$ has modulus $q_y$\nby the top-factor purity [lem-zl-affine-curve-hc2-purity].",
   "uses": [
    "thm-cbc-qbar",
    "lem-a1-affine-hc0",
    "lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual",
    "lem-zl-affine-curve-hc2-purity"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "The trace formula [cor-trf-point-counting] identifies the fiber\n$L$-function, i.e. the exponential of the point-count series of the\nfiber with coefficients $\\mathcal E$, with\n$P_1(T)/P_2(T)$ (the cohomological factorization over the finite\nfield $\\kappa(y)$, with $H_c^0=0$): exponentiating the alternating\ntrace sum degree by degree, the Euler-product identity\n[lem-zl-euler-product-identity] turns the exponential of the trace\nseries of $F$ on $H_c^i$ into $P_i(T)^{-1}$. Its Euler factors have real\ncoefficients by the $\\iota$-reality of $\\mathcal E$\n([def-wf-iota-real] applied to the restriction to the fiber), so\nthis quotient lies in $\\mathbf R(T)$. The radii are disjoint\n($|z|\\leq q_y^{1/2}$ for $P_1$, $|z|=q_y$ for the roots of\n$P_2$), and [lem-zl-root-radius-separation] therefore makes the\nfraction reduced with denominator $P_2$ in the reduced form; now\n[lem-zl-real-reduced-factors] gives\n$P_1,P_2\\in\\mathbf R[T]$. This holds for every $y$; degree zero is\ntrivial ($P_0=1$ by the vanishing), and all other degrees vanish or\nare captured by [lem-zl-affine-curve-range]. This proves the\nasserted $\\iota$-reality.",
   "uses": [
    "cor-trf-point-counting",
    "lem-zl-euler-product-identity",
    "def-wf-iota-real",
    "lem-zl-root-radius-separation",
    "lem-zl-real-reduced-factors",
    "lem-zl-affine-curve-range"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
